data.content:
Three things break in EF Core 10. Here's each issue and its fix:

---

### 1. `ExecuteUpdateAsync` — expression trees no longer accepted

The API now takes `Action<SetPropertyCalls<Blog>>` instead of `Expression<Func<...>>`. Your manual expression tree code won't compile. Replace it with a simple lambda:

```csharp
// .NET 10 — no expression trees needed
await context.Blogs.ExecuteUpdateAsync(s =>
{
    s.SetProperty(b => b.Views, 8);
    if (nameChanged)
    {
        s.SetProperty(b => b.Name, "foo");
    }
});
```

---

### 2. Complex type column names are now uniquified

Two changes affect your model:

- **Duplicate property names** (`ShippingAddress.Street` and `BillingAddress.Street`) — columns now get a numeric suffix to disambiguate. A migration will rename them.
- **Nested complex types** (`Order.Payment.BillingAddress.City`) — column name changes from `BillingAddress_City` to `Payment_BillingAddress_City` (full path).

**Fix:** Pin column names explicitly with `HasColumnName()`:

```csharp
modelBuilder.Entity<Customer>(b =>
{
    b.ComplexProperty(c => c.ShippingAddress, sa =>
        sa.Property(a => a.Street).HasColumnName("ShippingAddress_Street"));
    b.ComplexProperty(c => c.BillingAddress, ba =>
        ba.Property(a => a.Street).HasColumnName("BillingAddress_Street"));
});

// For nested complex types, preserve old names:
modelBuilder.Entity<Order>(b =>
{
    b.ComplexProperty(o => o.Payment, p =>
        p.ComplexProperty(pay => pay.BillingAddress, ba =>
            ba.Property(a => a.City).HasColumnName("BillingAddress_City")));
});
```

---

### 3. `IRelationalCommandDiagnosticsLogger` — new `logCommandText` parameter

All methods like `CommandReaderExecuting` now require an additional `string logCommandText` parameter:

```csharp
public class MyLogger : IRelationalCommandDiagnosticsLogger
{
    public InterceptionResult<DbDataReader> CommandReaderExecuting(
        IRelationalConnection connection,
        DbCommand command,
        DbContext context,
        Guid commandId,
        Guid connectionId,
        DateTimeOffset startTime,
        string logCommandText)   // ← new parameter (redacted SQL for logging)
    {
        // Use logCommandText for safe logging (constants may be redacted)
        // Use command.CommandText for actual SQL
    }
}
```

Update **every** method in your implementation — `CommandReaderExecuted`, `CommandScalarExecuting`, etc. all have the same new parameter.
